<Layouts.public locale={@locale} current={:method} alternates={@alternates}>
  <.section>
    <div class="prose stack gap-4">
      <p class="eyebrow">{gettext("Method")}</p>
      <h1 class="h1">{gettext("Where the figures come from.")}</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        {gettext(
          "Syli Atlas relies first on the IMF World Economic Outlook, published in April and October. Other sources only fill gaps and are always labelled."
        )}
      </p>

      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Every figure on the site names its source just below it. Syli Atlas is a non-commercial project: it uses each source within the terms below."
        )}
      </p>
    </div>
  </.section>

  <.section tight={:top}>
    <div class="stack gap-3" id="data-sources">
      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("Sources")}</h2>
      <p class="muted">{gettext("What each one provides, its terms and what is online")}</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <.card
          :for={s <- @data_sources}
          pad
          class="stack gap-2 source-card"
          id={"source-" <> s.id}
        >
          <h3 class="h2">
            <a :if={s.url} href={s.url} rel="noopener">{s.name}</a>
            <span :if={!s.url}>{s.name}</span>
          </h3>
          <p>{s.what}</p>
          <dl class="source-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>{gettext("Terms")}</dt>
              <dd>
                <a :if={s.terms_url} href={s.terms_url} rel="noopener">{s.terms}</a>
                <span :if={!s.terms_url}>{s.terms}</span>
              </dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>{gettext("Updated")}</dt>
              <dd>{s.updated}</dd>
            </div>
            <div :if={s.online}>
              <dt>{gettext("Online")}</dt>
              <dd>{s.online}</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </.card>
      </div>
    </div>
  </.section>

  <.section tight={:top}>
    <div class="prose stack gap-4">
      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("What Syli Atlas computes")}</h2>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "These figures are calculations, not data from a source. The page says so where they appear, and names the series they come from."
        )}
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>{gettext("Real GDP index, chained from the IMF growth rates.")}</li>
        <li>{gettext("Totals and averages of the regions and of Africa.")}</li>
        <li>
          {gettext(
            "UEMOA and CEMAC convergence criteria, checked against IMF figures. The IMF does not publish CEMAC's reference fiscal balance: that criterion is not computed."
          )}
        </li>
        <li>
          {gettext("The common rating scale (AAA = 22, default = 1) and the rating verdicts.")}
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("Daily updates")}</h2>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Every morning a job asks the IMF whether a new edition is out. When one is, the figures are imported, checked, published, and every profile is recomputed. Pages stay in your browser for one day and remain readable offline."
        )}
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("How totals are computed")}</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          {gettext("GDP and population of regions and of Africa are sums of their countries.")}
        </li>
        <li>
          {gettext("GDP per capita of a group is its total GDP divided by its population.")}
        </li>
        <li>
          {gettext(
            "Growth and inflation of a group are averages weighted by GDP in purchasing power parity."
          )}
        </li>
        <li>{gettext("Public debt of a group is weighted by GDP in dollars.")}</li>
        <li>
          {gettext(
            "The fiscal balance and the current account of a group are weighted by GDP in dollars. Groups have no unemployment rate: the IMF covers too few African countries."
          )}
        </li>
        <li>
          {gettext(
            "A country missing a value for a year is left out of the group for that year, and the page says so."
          )}
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("How changes are computed")}</h2>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Real GDP is an index chained from the IMF growth rates, so it measures output volume without inflation or exchange rate effects. Levels change in percent; rates (growth, inflation, debt) change in percentage points."
        )}
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2">{gettext("Estimates and projections")}</h2>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Recent years are IMF estimates, and later years are projections. Charts show them dashed. They are revised at every edition."
        )}
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" id="reuse">{gettext("Reuse")}</h2>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "What Syli Atlas computes and writes (regional and community totals, ranks, changes over a period, answer sentences, charts and share images) is under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence (CC BY 4.0): you may copy, adapt and republish it, commercial use included, as long as you credit Syli Atlas with a link to the page."
        )}
        <a href={SyliAtlasWeb.Seo.license_url()} rel="license">{gettext("Read the licence")}</a>
      </p>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Source figures keep the terms of their source, listed above: cite the IMF, the World Bank, CEPII or the agency along with Syli Atlas. Stock prices are the exception: their source (MansaAPI) allows display on this site only, so they are not covered by this licence and may not be redistributed."
        )}
      </p>
      <p class="small mono cite" id="reuse-example">
        {gettext(
          "Example: « Source: Syli Atlas (CC BY 4.0), from IMF, %{edition}, %{url} ».",
          edition: (@edition && @edition.label) || "World Economic Outlook",
          url: SyliAtlasWeb.Seo.url(Paths.area(@locale, "country", "senegal"))
        )}
      </p>
      <p>
        {gettext(
          "Every profile can be downloaded as CSV, and the JSON API is open: see the API page."
        )}
        <a href={Paths.api(@locale)}>{gettext("Public API")} →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </.section>
</Layouts.public>
